 html←GetStatistics dummy;folder;list
⍝ Returns the body of the usage data page: what the data is, a view of the newest data and the
⍝ files to download, as three tabs.
⍝ The files are offered newest first; see `ListUsageDataFiles`.
⍝ Every tab is a section with a heading of its own, so without JavaScript the page shows them one
⍝ below the other; Assets/JS/tabs.js turns them into tabs, the view being the first one shown.
 folder←∊P.LogFolder
 list←'zip'ListUsageDataFiles folder
 html←''
 :If 0=≢list
     html,←⊂'<p class="no-match">There is no usage data available yet.</p>'
 :Else
     html,←⊂'<div class="tabs" data-first-tab="view">'
     html,←⊂'<div class="tab-bar" role="tablist" aria-label="Usage data" hidden>'
     html,←⊂'<button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-info" aria-controls="info">Information</button>'
     html,←⊂'<button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-view" aria-controls="view">View</button>'
     html,←⊂'<button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-download" aria-controls="download">Downloads</button>'
     html,←⊂'</div>'
     html,←GetStatisticsInfo ⍬
     html,←GetStatisticsView folder(⊃list)
     html,←GetStatisticsDownloads folder list
     html,←⊂'</div>'
 :EndIf
⍝Done
